---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../../consts';
import homeAssistantMark from '../../icons/social/home-assistant-logomark-color-on-light.svg?url';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title={`My Home Assistant journey — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
      description="The independent Home Assistant chapter of my story, from apps and containers to Unraid and networking."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
      <a class="back" href="/about/">
        ← All chapters
      </a>
      <article>
        <header>
          <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT ME / INDEPENDENT JOURNEY</p>
          <h1>My Home Assistant journey</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Home Assistant was where my interest in connected devices turned
            into an interest in the systems behind them.
          </p>
          <div class="cover">
            <img
              src={homeAssistantMark}
              width="240"
              height="240"
              alt="Home Assistant logo"
            />
          </div>
        </header>
        <nav aria-label="In this chapter">
          <strong>In this chapter</strong>
          <a href="#starting-point">Starting point</a>
          <a href="#apps-and-services">Apps and services</a>
          <a href="#unraid-and-networking">Unraid and networking</a>
          <a href="#story-notes">Story notes</a>
        </nav>
        <section id="starting-point">
          <h2>Starting with the home</h2>
          <p>
            After years of exploring games, devices, and homebrew, I wanted to
            understand how the devices around me worked together. Home Assistant
            gave me a place to try that for myself. It moved my curiosity from
            individual devices to the connections and services that make a home
            feel responsive.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section id="apps-and-services">
          <h2>From “apps” to services</h2>
          <p>
            Docker helped me see that the tools I called apps could be services
            running in containers. That distinction changed how I thought about
            installing, updating, and connecting software. I was no longer only
            using an interface; I was learning what kept it running.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section id="unraid-and-networking">
          <h2>The systems underneath</h2>
          <p>
            Unraid gave me a place to bring services together. Routers, IP
            addresses, DNS, Wi-Fi, MAC addresses, and eventually VLANs became
            part of the same story: understanding why things could—or could
            not—talk to one another. That path led naturally toward deploying
            live websites.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section id="story-notes" class="story-notes">
          <h2>Details to add to this chapter</h2>
          <p>
            This is the beginning of the story. I still want to add the first
            device or automation that made Home Assistant click, the Docker
            setup that taught me the most, and the Unraid or network problem I
            remember solving. Those details belong here when I can tell them
            accurately.
          </p>
        </section>
      </article>
      <a class="back" href="/about/">
        ← Back to all chapters
      </a>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  main {
    width: min(920px, calc(100% - 32px));
    max-width: none;
    padding: 4rem 0 7rem;
  }
  article {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .back {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    color: light-dark(var(--brand-green-dark), var(--brand-green));
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 7vw, 5rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
  }
  h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .cover {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    min-height: 320px;
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
    border-radius: 24px;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #eafaff, #bde9fa);
  }
  .cover img {
    width: min(190px, 40vw);
    height: auto;
  }
  nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.3rem;
    border: 1px solid currentColor;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }
  nav strong {
    width: 100%;
  }
  nav a {
    color: light-dark(var(--brand-green-dark), var(--brand-green));
  }
  section {
    padding: 3rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #3c4659;
    scroll-margin-top: 5rem;
  }
  section p {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .story-notes {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  a:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid light-dark(var(--brand-green-dark), var(--brand-green));
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    main {
      padding-top: 2.5rem;
    }
    .cover {
      min-height: 240px;
    }
  }
</style>
